      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g of acetaminophen a day. That is a hepatotoxic dose, and for a 70 kg adult it's in the range where acetaminophen overdose is treated with N-acetylcysteine. You haven't given a clinical reason, and I don't know of any indication that would justify it.\n\nIf it helps, I can enter any of these right away:\n- **1000 mg** by mouth, 3 times daily (3 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** by mouth, 4 times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum for a healthy adult)\n- **650 mg** by mouth, 3 times daily\n- **500 mg** by mouth, 3 times daily\n\nIf 5000 mg was a typo, for example for 500 mg, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you believe this dose is clinically necessary, please talk with pharmacy or the attending first. They can review it and enter it through the appropriate override process."
      }
